    {
      "id": "ancient-narratives",
      "title": "Ancient Epics and Narrative Traditions",
      "role": "main",
      "parent": "periods",
      "summary": "Mesopotamian, Egyptian, Greek, Roman, and South Asian narratives. These are transmitted traditions with complex textual histories, not single verified events. New standalone readings of the Argonautica, Aeneid, Metamorphoses, and Nala and Damayanti complement the existing deep dives. The Gunditjmara/Budj Bim entry is an explicitly identified living oral tradition and landscape history, not an ancient written epic or a performed songline. The Klamath Llao and Skell entry treats a named Indigenous oral tradition through explicitly distinguished versions and separate geologic evidence.",
      "chapters": [
